summary:
- topic: FY2027 Budget
  text: The board discussed the challenging FY2027 budget, which faces a significant
    shortfall. Public forums revealed community desire for student-centered decisions
    and long-term fiscal stability. All current budget scenarios project a deficit,
    exacerbated by issues in the separate school nutrition fund.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The superintendent search is underway, with Zeal Education Group facilitating
    community feedback through on-site meetings and a Thought Exchange survey. The
    board voted to approve a one-time exception allowing student representatives to
    participate in semi-finalist interviews under strict confidentiality rules.
- topic: Elementary School Reconfiguration
  text: As a potential major cost-saving measure, the board unanimously voted to request
    a formal proposal from the superintendent on the benefits and impacts of reconfiguring
    the district's elementary schools. The board stressed the need for data and community
    input on this significant decision.
- topic: Community School Strategy
  text: The board approved the expansion of the Community School strategy to a district-wide
    model, starting with South Portland High School. This follows the model's success
    at the middle school and makes the district eligible for additional state and
    federal funding.
- topic: Financial Health and Audit
  text: The FY25 audit revealed a material weakness in reconciliation procedures.
    The Finance Director presented a multi-year plan to improve financial controls,
    noting that the school nutrition fund is projected to have a deficit over $1 million,
    which must be covered by the general school fund.
- topic: Immigration Community Support
  text: The board voted to formally endorse a South Portland City Council resolution
    supporting the local immigrant community in response to recent federal enforcement
    activities. Board members and staff were praised for their efforts to ensure student
    safety and wellbeing.
- topic: Athletic Complex Renovation
  text: An update was provided on the SPHS athletic complex renovation. The project
    includes a new eight-lane track, natural grass field, and restrooms, with construction
    planned to begin in April 2027 and a target completion of September 2027.
- topic: Pre-K Program Expansion
  text: The district is moving forward with the state's Child Development Services
    (CDS) transition, assuming responsibility for 4-year-olds with special education
    needs. The Pre-K lottery is open, and the district is pursuing partnerships with
    Head Start and other providers to expand available seats.
